## Container Best Practices

### Security
- Run as non-root user
- Use minimal base images (Alpine, Distroless)
- Scan images for vulnerabilities
- Sign images with cosign

### Performance
- Multi-stage builds
- Layer caching optimization
- `.dockerignore` to exclude unnecessary files
- Build arguments for environment-specific builds

### Podman Specific
- Rootless containers by default
- Use `podman-compose` for local development
- Volume management with `podman volume`
- Systemd integration for auto-restart

## Kubernetes Patterns

### Resource Management
- Set CPU/memory requests and limits
- Use Quality of Service classes
- Horizontal Pod Autoscaling
- Vertical Pod Autoscaling

### Deployment Strategies
- Blue-green (two complete environments)
- Canary (gradual traffic shift)
- Rolling update (pod-by-pod replacement)
- Recreate (downtime acceptable)

### Observability
- Prometheus for metrics
- Grafana for dashboards
- Loki for logs
- Tempo for traces
- Alertmanager for alerts

## CI/CD Pipelines

### GitHub Actions
- Matrix builds for multiple Python/Rust versions
- Caching dependencies between runs
- Security scanning in pipeline
- Automated testing on PRs

### GitLab CI
- Multi-stage pipelines
- Artifact management
- Environment deployments
- Review apps

### Deployment Automation
- Terraform for infrastructure
- Helm for Kubernetes deployments
- ArgoCD for GitOps
- FluxCD for continuous delivery

## Monitoring Stack

### Metrics
- Prometheus (collection)
- VictoriaMetrics (long-term storage)
- Thanos (global view)

### Visualization
- Grafana (dashboards)
- Kibana (logs visualization)

### Logging
- Loki (log aggregation)
- Fluentd/Fluent Bit (log collection)
- Elasticsearch (alternative)

### Tracing
- Jaeger
- Tempo
- OpenTelemetry

### Alerting
- Alertmanager
- OpsGenie/PagerDuty integration
- Slack/Teams notifications

## Disaster Recovery

### Backup Strategies
- 3-2-1 rule: 3 copies, 2 media types, 1 offsite
- Database backups (logical + physical)
- Configuration backups
- Secret backups (encrypted)

### Recovery Objectives
- RTO (Recovery Time Objective): [X hours]
- RPO (Recovery Point Objective): [Y minutes]

### Testing
- Regular disaster recovery drills
- Chaos engineering (Chaos Monkey)
- Failover testing

## Cost Optimization

### Compute
- Spot instances for batch workloads
- Reserved instances for steady-state
- Auto-scaling to match demand
- Right-sizing instances

### Storage
- Lifecycle policies (move to cheaper storage)
- Compression and deduplication
- Cleanup old/unused data

### Network
- CDN for static assets
- Compression (gzip, brotli)
- Caching at multiple levels

### Monitoring
- Cost allocation tags
- Budget alerts
- Regular cost reviews
